// Engine test chapter 1. Exercises text, expressions, stats, flags, conditions,
// choices (with [once] and conditions), calls, and chapter flow. Not part of the story.
// Version 2: scratch variables renamed with a leading underscore (the flag registry rule).
@chapter et1
@title Engine Test: Basics
@book engine-test
@version 2
@next et2

# start
## Basics
This is a plain line of text.
Interpolation works: gold is {_gold} and hunger is {hunger}.
$ _gold = 5
$ _gold += 3
$ flag _seen_intro
Now gold is {_gold}, and the flag reads {_seen_intro}.
---
?if _gold >= 8 and _seen_intro
  Condition passed.
?elif _gold >= 5
  Middle branch.
?else
  Condition failed.
?end
$ hunger += 200
Hunger was clamped to {hunger}.
-> doors

# doors
Two doors stand ahead.
* Take the left door
  $ et.door = "left"
  $ cunning_brutal -= 10
  You went left.
* Take the right door [once]
  $ et.door = "right"
  $ cunning_brutal += 10
  You went right.
  -> doors
* Open the secret door ?if _gold > 100
  This should never appear.
Both paths rejoin here.
~> helper
Back from the helper. Counter is {_counter}.
:before_finale
---
-> finale

# helper
$ _counter += 1
Inside the helper, counter is {_counter}.
<~

# finale
$ _roll_result = roll(6)
A seeded roll gave {_roll_result}. The doors scene ran {visited("doors")} time(s).
=> next
